user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-02-10T16:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T14:34:26Z","closed_at":"2026-05-21T14:34:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.stable\n- Not reproducible in 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nMac OS 26.2 - iOS 26.2.1 - Godot 4.6.stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn iOS, when enumerating a directory using `ResourceLoader.list_directory()` the bundle root contents is returned. It seems like any path gets resolved to `res://`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. List a sub-directory using `ResourceLoader.list_directory()` in the editor, result: contents is shown.\n2. Do the same in a project export for iOS, result: bundle root contents is shown.\n\nSee _Minimal reproduction project_.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n1. Open attached project\n2. Set up the iOS export (default settings, you only need to set `App Store Team ID` and `Bundle Identifier`\n3. Run the project in the editor, result: both the specific files (using `DirAccess.file_exists()`) are found and the directory contents (using `ResourceLoader.list_directory()`) is listed.\n4. Run the project with Xcode on an iOS device (tested on iPhone 13 Pro running iOS 26.2.1), result: the specific files are found, but the directory contents is NOT listed (instead, bundle root is displayed).\n\n[ios-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25215151/ios-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars